PROBLEM STATEMENT:
Given an integer array nums and an integer val, remove all occurrences of val from the array in-place. Return the number 
of elements that are not equal to val.The first k elements of the array should contain all elements that are not equal to val, where k is the returned value.
AIM:To write a Java program that removes all occurrences of a given value from an integer array in-place and returns the number of remaining elements.
JAVA CODE:
class Solution {
    public int removeElement(int[] nums, int val) {
        int k = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
            if (nums[i] != val) {
                nums[k] = nums[i];
                k++;
            }
        }

        return k;
    }
}
INPUT:
nums = [3, 2, 2, 3]
val = 3
OUTPUT:
2
